Krita Nova 47 - Import Brushes: Procreate brushes, Krita presets and bundles

"Import Brushes..." (patch 42) opens more than Photoshop brushes now:

- Procreate .brush / .brushset (zip archives): every brush becomes a Pixel
  brush preset, in a category named after the file. From Brush.archive (an
  NSKeyedArchiver binary property list): name, size (paintSize x maxSize),
  spacing (plotSpacing), opacity (maxOpacity), pen pressure on size and
  opacity (dynamicsPressureSize / Opacity), size and opacity jitter
  (dynamicsJitterSize / Opacity), rotation jitter (shapeScatter), scatter
  (plotJitter). Shape.png becomes a PNG tip (white is paint, or black with
  shapeInverted; transparent is no paint; at most 1024 px); without one (a
  shape built into Procreate) the brush gets a round tip. brushset.plist
  gives the order. Procreate's scales are not published: these mappings
  follow what is known of them. Not carried over: grain, taper, tilt, speed,
  wet mixing, blend modes.
- Krita presets (.kpp): imported into the category "Imported Brushes".
- Krita bundles (.bundle): installed like Settings > Manage Resource
  Libraries > Import does; their presets also get a category named after the
  file. The same bundle again is not installed twice.
- Without a known extension (Android document names) the format is told by
  the contents.

KisProcreateBrushReader (zip via QuaZip, binary and XML property lists,
NSKeyedArchiver references). KisAbrPresetImporter: the preset builder and
tagging are shared by Photoshop and Procreate brushes; importFile().
